  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HONDURAS TRANSPORTATION AND FREIGHT LOGISTICS SECTOR REFORM Program</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Programa de Reformas del Sector Transporte y Logstica de Carga de Honduras</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El objetivo del programa es contribuir a la mejora del desempeo logstico de Hondurasa travs de reformas sectoriales en los mbitos regulatorio, institucional, de planificacin y de facilitacin comercial, que permita ganancias en la competitividad e integracin regional. Los objetivos especficos del programa son: (i) consolidar unmarco normativo con reglamentos especficos para la mejora de servicios de logstica de carga con visin de largo plazo;(ii) el fortalecimiento de la institucionalidad del sector logstico a travs de la creacin del Consejo Nacional de Logstica (CNL)e instancia a nivel tcnico; (iii) la mejora de la planificacin integral en el sector y la prestacin de servicios asociados; y (iv) lamodernizacin y simplificacin de los procesos y los sistemas tecnolgicos de facilitacin comercial. El presente prstamo es el primero de una serie de tres operaciones, vinculadas tcnicamente entre s, pero financiadasen forma independiente, bajo la modalidad de Prstamo Programtico de Apoyo a Reformas de Polticas (CS-3633-2).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program&apos;s objective is to support improvements in Honduras&apos;s logistics performance through regulatory, institutional, planning, and trade facilitation reforms in the sector, with a view to boosting competitiveness and regional integration. The specific objectives are to: (i) develop a regulatory framework with specific rules aimed at improving freight logistics services as part of a long-term vision; (ii) strengthen the institutional framework for the logistics sector by creating the National Logistics Council and a technical entity; (iii) improve integrated planning in the sector and delivery of the associated services; and (iv) modernize and simplify trade facilitation processes and technological systems.This loan is the first in a series of three operations that are technically linked but financed separately as programmatic policy-based loan operations (document CS-3633-2).</narrative>
  </description>
